; trig: tell the game where the music is. (trig N) writes id N (0-63) to the
; track's status byte; the game polls MMLisp_trig(track) and reacts to any
; change: flash on the downbeat, open the door at the end of the phrase...
; The same id firing again still counts, so a cue inside a loop fires on
; every pass. In the live app each cue is written to the log as it passes.
(import "presets/gm/set.mmlisp")

(fm1 :tempo 120 :oct 4 :len 4 gm-organ-perc
  (trig 1) c e g e          ; 1: intro
  #verse
  (trig 2) f a > c < a      ; 2: fires on both passes
  (trig 3) g b > d < b
  (go verse 2)
  (trig 4) :len 1 c)        ; 4: the end
